# Vercel ignores .gitignore — list local-only artifacts here so `eve deploy`
# doesn't sweep 100+ MB of dev-runtime state into every upload.

# eve durable-workflow runtime state written during local dev runs (~106 MB).
# Regenerated locally; never belongs in a deployment.
.workflow-data

# eve's local runtime/cache dir — grows into the GBs across dev runs. Vercel
# builds the agent itself (`npx eve build`), so this is pure local state. Left
# in, its file COUNT alone overflows the 10 MB deployment-manifest limit and the
# deploy fails with "Request body too large" long before any bytes upload.
.eve

# Local build outputs. Vercel runs the build remotely, so uploading ours is
# waste: `.output` is `eve build`'s (~49 MB), `dist/` is the Vite front-end
# (the Worker serves that, not this project).
.output
dist

# The Cloudflare Worker backend + its node_modules — a separate deploy target.
worker

# Other deploy targets / platforms that share this repo but not this project:
# the Expo app (~1.5 GB with its node_modules) and the Vercel render function.
mobile-app
render-fn

# Agent/skill tooling for local Claude Code sessions.
.claude

# Local media / test renders that don't belong in the agent deployment.
public/media
